"1034","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1034 Arabic Hadees: 2082"
"1035","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: ""The Angel of Death came to me—and in another version: 'The Angel of Death comes to people visibly'—until he came to Moses (peace be upon him) and said: 'Answer your Lord.' So Moses (peace be upon him) struck the eye of the Angel of Death and gouged it out. The angel returned to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and said: 'O Lord! You sent me to a servant of Yours who does not want death, and he has gouged out my eye (and were it not for his honor upon You, I would have caused him distress).' So Allah restored his eye to him and said: 'Return to My servant and say to him: Do you want life? If you want life, then place your hand on the back of an ox, and whatever hairs your hand covers, you will live for a year for each hair.' He said: 'O Lord! Then what?' He said: 'Then death.' He said: 'Then let it be now.' He said: 'O Lord, cause me to die near the Sacred Land, a stone's throw away.' (He said: 'So he smelled it a sniff and his soul was taken.' He said: 'Then after that he came to people secretly.') The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: 'By Allah, if I were there, I would show you his grave beside the road, at—and in the version: beneath the red sand dune.'"""
"1036","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1036 Arabic Hadees: 804"
"1037","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1037 Arabic Hadees: 2138"
"1038","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1038 Arabic Hadees: 2464"
"1039","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1039 Arabic Hadees: 805"
"1040","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1040 Arabic Hadees: 605"
"1041","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1041 Arabic Hadees: 2551"
"1042","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I went out one night and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) walking alone, with no one with him. I thought that he disliked having anyone walk with him. So I began walking in the shadow of the moon. He turned around, saw me, and said: ""Who is this?"" I said: ""Abu Dharr, may Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""O Abu Dharr, come here."" So I walked with him for a while, and he said: ""The most abundant (in wealth) are the least (in reward) on the Day of Resurrection, except for one whom Allah gives wealth and he spends it to his right, left, in front of him, and behind him, and does good with it."" Then I walked with him for a while, and he said to me: ""Sit here."" He made me sit in a depression surrounded by stones. He said to me: ""Sit here until I return to you."" He went off into the rocky ground (al-harrah) until I could no longer see him. He stayed away from me for a long time. Then I heard him as he was returning, saying: ""Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery!"" When he came, I could not restrain myself until I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me a ransom for you, who were you speaking to in the rocky ground? I did not hear anyone reply to you."" He said: ""That was Gabriel (peace be upon him). He met me in the rocky ground and said: 'Give glad tidings to your nation that whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.' I said: 'O Gabriel, even if he stole and even if he committed adultery?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery?' He said: 'Yes, and even if he drank wine.'"""
"1043","Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan, performs the prayers, and performs Hajj to the House — I do not know whether he mentioned zakat or not — it becomes a right upon Allah to forgive him, whether he emigrates in the cause of Allah or remains in the land where he was born.""Mu'adh said: ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I not inform the people of this?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave the people to work, for in Paradise there are one hundred degrees; the distance between each two degrees is like the distance between the heaven and the earth. And Al-Firdaws is the highest part of Paradise and its middle, and above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it spring forth the rivers of Paradise. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaws."""
"1044","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1044 Arabic Hadees: 2437"
"1045","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1045 Arabic Hadees: 3065"
"1046","On the authority of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form. He said: 'In what does the Highest Assembly (of angels) dispute?' I said: 'I do not know.' So He placed His Hand between my shoulders until I felt the coolness of His fingertips between my breast. Then He said: 'In what does the Highest Assembly dispute?' I said: 'Regarding the expiations (kaffārāt) and the degrees (darajāt).' He said: 'And what are the expiations?' I said: 'Perfecting the ablution (wuḍūʾ) during difficulties, walking on foot to the congregational prayers, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.' He said: 'Then what are the degrees?' I said: 'Feeding food, spreading the greeting of peace (salām), and praying at night while people are asleep.' He said: 'Speak.' I said: 'What shall I say?' He said: 'Say: O Allah! I ask You for the performance of good deeds, the abandonment of evil deeds, and if You intend a trial (fitnah) for a people while I am among them, then take me to You without being afflicted (by that trial).'"""
"1047","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1047 Arabic Hadees: 43"
"1048","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1048 Arabic Hadees: 688"
