"1052","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1052 Arabic Hadees: 129"
"1053","From Abu Abdur-Rahman Al-Juhani, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), two riders appeared. When he saw them, he said: ""Two Kindis from Madh'hij."" When they reached him, they were men from Madh'hij. One of them approached to pledge allegiance to him. When he took his hand, he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about someone who saw you, believed in you, believed you, and followed you?"" He said: ""Glad tidings for him."" So he wiped his hand and turned away. Then the other came forward until he took his hand to pledge allegiance. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about someone who believed in you, believed you, and followed you but did not see you?"" He said: ""Glad tidings for him, then glad tidings for him, then glad tidings for him."" So he wiped his hand and turned away."
"1054","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1054 Arabic Hadees: 2202"
"1055","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1055 Arabic Hadees: 130"
