"1091","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1091 Arabic Hadees: 911"
"1092","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were on a military expedition when a man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar. The Ansari said: ""O Ansar!"" And the Muhajir said: ""O Muhajirun!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""What is this call of the Days of Ignorance?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar."" He said: ""Leave it, for it is foul."" (Jabir said: The Ansar were more numerous when the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) arrived, then the Muhajirun increased later.) Abdullah ibn Ubayy heard of it and said: ""Have they done so?! By Allah, if we return to Medina, the more honorable will surely expel the more humble from it."" Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Leave him, lest people say that Muhammad kills his companions."""
"1093","On the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and went on a military expedition with him. I found myself behind the best of people that day, until they killed the children. And he said once: ""the offspring."" That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he said: ""What is the matter with a people that killing has passed them by today until they killed the children?"" A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! They are only the children of the polytheists."" He said: ""Behold, the best of you are the sons of polytheists."" Then he said: ""Behold, do not kill children. Behold, do not kill children."" He said: ""Every soul is born upon the fitrah until its tongue speaks for it, then its parents make it Jewish or make it Christian."""
"1094","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1094 Arabic Hadees: 1275"
"1095","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1095 Arabic Hadees: 2484"
"1096","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1096 Arabic Hadees: 1139"
"1097","Abdur-Rahman bin Jubair bin Nufair narrated from his father who said: We sat with Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad one day, and a man passed by him and said: ""Blessed are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, we wished we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed."" So he became angry, and I was surprised that he said nothing but good. Then he turned to him and said: ""What makes a man wish for a presence that Allah has kept him away from, not knowing how he would have been in it had he witnessed it?! By Allah, there were people who were present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whom Allah threw on their faces in Hellfire; they did not respond to him nor believe him. Do you not praise Allah that He brought you out knowing none but your Lord, believing in what your Prophet brought, having been spared the trial by others? By Allah, Allah sent the Prophet ﷺ in the most severe condition any prophet was sent in, during a period (of ignorance) and Jahiliyyah where they saw no religion better than worshipping idols. He brought a Criterion (Furqan) that separated between truth and falsehood, and separated between a father and his son, until a man would see his father, his son, or his brother as a disbeliever, while Allah had opened the lock of his heart to faith. He knows that if he perishes he will enter the Fire, so his eye finds no rest while he knows his beloved is in the Fire. And this is what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And those who say: Our Lord! Grant us from our wives and our offspring the comfort of our eyes' (Al-Furqan: 74)."""
"1098","When Yazid ibn al-Muhallab was appointed governor of Khurasan, he said: ""Direct me to a man who is complete in the qualities of goodness."" He was directed to Abu Burdah ibn Abu Musa al-Ash'ari. When he came to him, he saw a man of surpassing appearance; and when he spoke with him, he found his inner reality better than his outward appearance. He said: ""I have appointed you over such-and-such of my affairs."" He sought exemption, but he refused to exempt him. He said: ""O Commander! Shall I not inform you of something my father narrated to me, that he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""Bring it forth."" He said: ""He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Whoever assumes a position of authority while knowing that he is not fit for that position, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"" He said: ""And I bear witness, O Commander, that I am not fit for what you have called me to."" Yazid said to him: ""You have only incited me against yourself and increased my desire for you. Go forth to your covenant, for I will not exempt you."" Then he went out (the original text says: 'then he went out,' but perhaps the correct reading is: 'he went out, then') and remained in it as long as Allah willed. Then he sought permission to return to him, and he granted him permission. He said: ""O Commander! Shall I not narrate to you something my father narrated to me, that he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""Bring it forth."" He said: ""Cursed is he who asks by the Face of Allah, and cursed is he who is asked by the Face of Allah and then refuses his petitioner what he did not ask for out of arrogance."" He said: ""And I ask you by the Face of Allah, O Commander, that you exempt me from your work."" So he exempted him."
